L001256	\section{Constraint on the phases in the EFD due to positivity}\label{sec:positivity}
L001257	In this section, we derive a constraint on the possible anyon condensates in the EFD $\kket{\rho}$ due to the positivity of the density matrix $\rho$.
L001258	
L001259	We show that the composite object $\alpha\bar{\beta}$ can condense in $\kket{\rho}$ only if the anyon $\alpha\bar{\alpha}$, $\alpha\bar{\beta}$, and $\beta\bar{\beta}$ do not have mutual statistics.
L001260	
L001261	This constraint does not affect the classification of the phases induced by incoherent errors studied in the main text.
L001262	
L001263	Those phases feature condensed paired anyon $\alpha\bar{\alpha}$ in the EFD and do not violate this constraint.
L001264	
L001265	The constraint plays a role when analyzing the possible anyon condensates induced by the coherent errors.
L001266	
L001267	A similar constraint on the symmetry-protected topological phases in 1D mixed states due to positivity is derived in Ref.~\cite{Duivenvoorden:2017cha}.
L001268	
L001269	We here provide a derivation.
L001270	
L001271	Suppose $\alpha\bar{\beta}$ is condensed in $\kket{\rho}$, the open string operator $W_{\alpha\bar{\beta}}(\calP)$ along a path $\calP$ acquires a non-vanishing expectation value when the endpoints of $\calP$ are faraway, i.e.
L001272	\begin{align}
L001273	    \left|\langle\!\langle W_{\alpha\overline{\beta}}(\calP)\rangle\!\rangle\right| = \left|\frac{\bbra{\rho} W_{\alpha\overline{\beta}}(\calP) \kket{\rho}}{\bbrakket{\rho}{\rho}}\right| = \left|\frac{\tr\rho\, w_\alpha(\calP)\, \rho\, w_\beta^\dagger(\calP)}{\tr \rho^2}\right| > 0.
L001274	\end{align}
L001275	Due to the positivity of density matrix $\rho$, one can define the square root of $\rho$ such that $\rho = \sqrt{\rho}\sqrt{\rho}$. We then have
L001276	\begin{align}
L001277	    0<\left|\langle\!\langle W_{\alpha\overline{\beta}}(\calP)\rangle\!\rangle\right|^2 &= \left|\frac{\tr \sqrt{\rho}\,w_\alpha(\calP)\, \sqrt{\rho}\, \sqrt{\rho}\, w_\beta^\dagger(\calP)\,\sqrt{\rho}}{\tr \rho^2}\right|^2 \nonumber \\
L001278	    &\leq \frac{\tr \sqrt{\rho}\,w_\alpha(\calP)\, \sqrt{\rho}\, \sqrt{\rho}\, w_\alpha^\dagger(\calP)\,\sqrt{\rho}}{\tr \rho^2} \,\frac{\tr \sqrt{\rho}\,w_\beta(\calP)\, \sqrt{\rho}\, \sqrt{\rho}\, w_\beta^\dagger(\calP)\,\sqrt{\rho}}{\tr \rho^2} \nonumber \\
L001279	    &= \langle\!\langle W_{\alpha\overline{\alpha}}(\calP)\rangle\!\rangle \langle\!\langle W_{\beta\overline{\beta}}(\calP)\rangle\!\rangle
L001280	\end{align}
L001281	Here, we use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality in the second line.
L001282	
L001283	The inequality indicates that $W_{\alpha\overline{\alpha}}$ and $W_{\beta\overline{\beta}}$ are also non-decaying, i.e. the paired anyons $\alpha\bar{\alpha}$ and $\beta\bar{\beta}$ are condensed.
L001284	
L001285	In the case that $\alpha\bar{\alpha}$, $\alpha\bar{\beta}$, and $\beta\bar{\beta}$ have non-trivial mutual statistics, the condensate of this triad cannot exist.
L001286	
