L001790	
L001791	Allowing coherent errors may lead to additional gapped phases beyond the above five possibilities.
L001792	
L001793	For example, we consider the amplitude-damping channel
L001794	\begin{align}
L001795	\calK_{1,i} = \frac{1+\sqrt{1-\kappa}}{2}\bbI + \frac{1-\sqrt{1-\kappa}}{2} Z_i, \quad \calK_{2,i} =  \frac{\sqrt{\kappa}}{2}(X_i+\ri Y_i).
L001796	\end{align}
L001797	The channel can generate $e, \bar{e}, m, \bar{m}, e\bar{m}, m\bar{e}$ in the EFD, which cannot be created by incoherent errors.
